IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Passports Act 2005 (Commonwealth) -- the citizen's entitlement to a passport (s 7), the Minister's satisfaction of
-- citizenship and identity (s 8), the definition of a child (s 6(1)), the bar on issuing to a child without the consent of each
-- person with parental responsibility or a court order, its exceptions and the meaning of parental responsibility (s 11), the
-- mandatory and discretionary refusal grounds as inputs (ss 12, 14, 15, 16, 17), when a travel document is valid (s 20), and which
-- decisions are reviewable (s 48).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 21, compilation date 8 November 2025 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 60, 2025"; register id C2025C00643),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2005A00005.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0014 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl: priority 1, raised 5 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives (chloe c013 2011-06-01, c068 2031-06-10; jake k012 2016-06-15, k035 2026-05-10; daniel d036 2027-06-14).
-- They ask: who may apply for a child's passport and whose consent is needed (s 11) -- Chloe at 8, Jake at 9, Oliver and Anjali as
-- babies, Anjali born in London; and what a 19-year-old needs (s 8). SCOPED to ss 7, 8 and 11 first, with the definitions,
-- conditions and exceptions needed to answer them (ss 6(1) "child", 12, 14-17, 20, 48).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: travel-related documents (ss 9, 10) beyond the word "Australian travel document"; the competent authorities and the
-- grounds on which they make refusal/cancellation requests (ss 12-14, 16, 18-19) -- only the request's effect is encoded, as an
-- INPUT; refusal to process for fraud (s 19A) beyond its reviewability; cancellation, suspension and surrender (ss 22-26); the
-- offences (Part 4); information disclosure (ss 42-47); the form, name and signature rules (s 53); fees, which are imposed by the
-- Australian Passports (Application Fees) Act 2005 and not stated in this Act (INPUT: "accompanied by the applicable fee"); and every
-- Minister's determination (s 57), including the one that sets when a passport ceases to be valid (s 20(2)) -- not retrieved, so the
-- expiry date is an INPUT. s 11 was amended in 2006 and 2015 (Endnote 4); events before the 2015 amendment (Chloe, 2011) are read
-- here against the 2025 text, which may differ from the text then in force.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example encodings. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Australian Passports Act 2005`

§§ `6(1) -- child`

-- s 6(1): "child means a person who is under 18 and who has never been married."
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `has ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child under s 6(1)` IF
    `age in years` < 18 AND (NOT `has ever been married`)

§§ `11(5) -- parental responsibility`

-- s 11(5): "a person has parental responsibility for a child if, and only if: (a) the person: (i) is the child's parent (including a
-- person who is presumed to be the child's parent because of a presumption (other than in section 69Q) in ... the Family Law Act
-- 1975); and (ii) has not ceased to have parental responsibility for the child because of an order made under the Family Law Act
-- 1975; or (aa) the person: (i) is the child's parent (including ... a presumption (other than in section 189) in ... the Family
-- Court Act 1997 (WA)); and (ii) has not ceased to have parental responsibility for the child because of an order made under that
-- Act; or (b) under a parenting order: (i) the child is to live with the person; or (ii) the person has parental responsibility for
-- the child; or (d) the person has guardianship or custody of, or has parental responsibility for, the child under a law of the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory."
--
-- Read literally, (a) and (aa) are alternatives: a parent whose responsibility was removed by an order under one Act still satisfies
-- the other limb unless an order under that Act removed it too. That is what is encoded. (Whether a court would read (a) and (aa) as
-- covering different children -- the Family Law Act for some WA children, the Family Court Act 1997 (WA) for others -- is an
-- inference not tested here.)
DECLARE `Person facts` HAS
    `is the child's parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parental responsibility removed by a Family Law Act 1975 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parental responsibility removed by a Family Court Act 1997 (WA) order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is to live with them under a parenting order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has parental responsibility under a parenting order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has guardianship, custody or parental responsibility under another law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A `Person facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has parental responsibility under s 11(5)` IF
        (`p`'s `is the child's parent` AND (NOT `p`'s `parental responsibility removed by a Family Law Act 1975 order`))
    OR  (`p`'s `is the child's parent` AND (NOT `p`'s `parental responsibility removed by a Family Court Act 1997 (WA) order`))
    OR  `p`'s `the child is to live with them under a parenting order`
    OR  `p`'s `has parental responsibility under a parenting order`
    OR  `p`'s `has guardianship, custody or parental responsibility under another law`

§§ `20 -- when a travel document is valid`

-- s 20(1): "An Australian travel document ceases to be valid: (a) in accordance with a determination made for the purposes of
-- subsection (2); or (b) at the time specified on the document; or (c) when cancelled under this Division; whichever happens first."
-- (3): "An Australian travel document is not valid while it is suspended under section 22A." Dates are written YYYYMMDD; a document
-- is treated as having ceased ON the date specified on it (an inference about "at the time specified").
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER,
      `the date specified on the document` IS A NUMBER,
      `ceased under a Minister's determination` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the travel document is valid under s 20` IF
        `the date` < `the date specified on the document`
    AND (NOT `ceased under a Minister's determination`)
    AND (NOT `cancelled`)
    AND (NOT `suspended`)

§§ `7, 8, 11, 12, 14-17 -- an application for a passport`

DECLARE `Passport application` HAS
    `application date` IS A NUMBER
    `age at application` IS A NUMBER
    `has ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied the person is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied of the person's identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the approved form with the applicable fee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `persons with parental responsibility` IS A NUMBER
    `of them, persons who consent` IS A NUMBER
    `a court order permits the document, international travel, or living or spending time with someone outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special circumstances in a Minister's determination exist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied the child's welfare would be adversely affected without travel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied the child urgently needs to travel because of a family crisis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no non-consenting person can be contacted within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has departed Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months from departing Australia to the application` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister considers a document should issue to enable return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a refusal/cancellation request under s 12(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `already holds an Australian travel document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date specified on that document` IS A NUMBER
    `that document has ceased under a determination or been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that document is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Minister's determination permits a further document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a refusal/cancellation request under s 14(1) or 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before the application` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister exercises a discretion to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is a child` IF
    `is a child under s 6(1)` (`a`'s `age at application`) (`a`'s `has ever been married`)

-- s 11(1): "The Minister must not issue an Australian travel document to a child unless: (a) each person who has parental
-- responsibility for the child consents to the child having an Australian travel document; or (b) an order of a court of the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory permits: (i) the child to have an Australian travel document; or (ii) the child to travel
-- internationally; or (iii) the child to live or spend time with another person who is outside Australia."
-- "Each person" is read literally: if no-one has parental responsibility, (a) is met.
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(1) consent or a court order is in place` IF
        `a`'s `of them, persons who consent` >= `a`'s `persons with parental responsibility`
    OR  `a`'s `a court order permits the document, international travel, or living or spending time with someone outside Australia`

-- s 11(2): "Subsection (1) does not prevent the Minister from issuing ... if: (a) circumstances specified in a Minister's
-- determination as special circumstances exist; or (b) the Minister is satisfied that the child's welfare (physical or psychological)
-- would be adversely affected if the child were not able to travel internationally; or (c) the Minister is satisfied that: (i) the
-- child urgently needs to travel internationally because of a family crisis; and (ii) if there is a person who has parental
-- responsibility for the child and who has not consented ... -- it is not possible to contact that person within a reasonable period;
-- or (d) in the case of a child who is outside Australia -- the child departed Australia less than 12 months before the application
-- ... was made and the Minister considers that an Australian travel document should be issued to enable the child's return to
-- Australia."
-- These are permissions ("does not prevent"), not duties. (d) needs a departure: a child born abroad who has never been in Australia
-- cannot use it.
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in s 11(2) is available` IF
        `a`'s `special circumstances in a Minister's determination exist`
    OR  `a`'s `the Minister is satisfied the child's welfare would be adversely affected without travel`
    OR  (`a`'s `the Minister is satisfied the child urgently needs to travel because of a family crisis`
         AND `a`'s `no non-consenting person can be contacted within a reasonable period`)
    OR  (    `a`'s `is outside Australia`
         AND `a`'s `has departed Australia`
         AND `a`'s `months from departing Australia to the application` < 12
         AND `a`'s `the Minister considers a document should issue to enable return`)

GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11 bars the issue` IF
        `the applicant is a child` `a`
    AND (NOT `s 11(1) consent or a court order is in place` `a`)
    AND (NOT `an exception in s 11(2) is available` `a`)

-- s 17(1): "The Minister must not issue an Australian travel document to a person if the person has already been issued with an
-- Australian travel document and that document is still valid or is suspended under section 22A." (2): not if a Minister's
-- determination specifies the circumstances.
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 bars the issue` IF
        `a`'s `already holds an Australian travel document`
    AND (    `the travel document is valid under s 20` (`a`'s `application date`) (`a`'s `date specified on that document`)
                 (`a`'s `that document has ceased under a determination or been cancelled`) FALSE (`a`'s `that document is suspended`)
         OR  `a`'s `that document is suspended`)
    AND (NOT `a`'s `a Minister's determination permits a further document`)

-- s 8: "Before issuing an Australian passport to a person, the Minister must be satisfied: (a) that the person is an Australian
-- citizen; and (b) of the identity of the person."
-- s 12(2): if a competent authority makes a request under s 12(1) (arrest warrant; prevented from travelling) or (1A) (reportable
-- offender), "the Minister must not issue an Australian passport to the person".
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must not issue the passport` IF
        (NOT `a`'s `the Minister is satisfied the person is a citizen`)
    OR  (NOT `a`'s `the Minister is satisfied of the person's identity`)
    OR  `s 11 bars the issue` `a`
    OR  `a`'s `a refusal/cancellation request under s 12(1) or (1A)`
    OR  `s 17 bars the issue` `a`

-- s 14(2), 16(2): after a request "the Minister may refuse"; s 15: "The Minister may refuse ... if ... in the 5 years before the
-- application is made, 2 or more Australian travel documents issued to the person have been lost or stolen."
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may refuse the passport` IF
        `a`'s `a refusal/cancellation request under s 14(1) or 16(1)`
    OR  `a`'s `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before the application` >= 2

-- s 7(1): "An Australian citizen is entitled, on application to the Minister, to be issued with an Australian passport by the
-- Minister." (2): the entitlement "is affected by section 8 and by Division 2". (3): the application must be "(a) made in the form
-- approved by the Minister; and (b) accompanied by the applicable fee (if any)".
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is entitled to the passport` IF
        `a`'s `is an Australian citizen`
    AND `a`'s `made in the approved form with the applicable fee`
    AND (NOT `the Minister must not issue the passport` `a`)
    AND (NOT (`the Minister may refuse the passport` `a` AND `a`'s `the Minister exercises a discretion to refuse`))

§§ `48 -- reviewable decisions`

-- s 48: reviewable decisions include "(a) a decision to issue an Australian travel document, other than: (i) a decision made under
-- paragraph 9(1A)(b); or (ii) a decision to issue an Australian travel document to a child; (b) a decision to refuse to issue an
-- Australian travel document (other than a decision in relation to which a declaration under subsection 11(3) has been made or a
-- decision made because of subsection 12(2)); (c) a decision to cancel an Australian travel document (other than under section
-- 22AA); (ca) a decision to refuse to process an application".
-- s 11(3): on refusing a child, "the Minister may declare that he or she is refusing to exercise the discretion under subsection (2)
-- because the matter should be dealt with by a court."
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `issue to an adult`
    `issue to a child`
    `refusal to issue`
    `cancellation under s 22`
    `cancellation under s 22AA`
    `refusal to process an application`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `a s 11(3) declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `made because of s 12(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is reviewable under s 48` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `issue to an adult` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `issue to a child` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusal to issue` THEN (NOT `a s 11(3) declaration was made`) AND (NOT `made because of s 12(2)`)
    WHEN `cancellation under s 22` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancellation under s 22AA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusal to process an application` THEN TRUE
